## Bandit Level 14 → Level 15

**Challenge:** 
The password for the next level can be retrieved by submitting the password of the current level to port 30000 on localhost.

**Solution:**
bandit14@bandit:/etc/bandit_pass$ cat bandit14
MU4VWeTyJk8ROof1qqmcBPaLh7lDCPvS
bandit14@bandit:/etc/bandit_pass$ cd /
bandit14@bandit:/$ cd ~
bandit14@bandit:~$ telnet localhost 30000
Trying 127.0.0.1...
Connected to localhost.
Escape character is '^]'.
MU4VWeTyJk8ROof1qqmcBPaLh7lDCPvS
Correct!
8xCjnmgoKbGLhHFAZlGE5Tmu4M2tKJQo

**Explanation:**
I first had to go into the directory where the password for this level was located as that was needed to input to get the password for the next level.

Once I had that I used the telnet command and connected to port 30000 on localhost and put the password in to get the password for the next level.

**Password:**
8xCjnmgoKbGLhHFAZlGE5Tmu4M2tKJQo

**What I learned:**
I learned how to connect to ports using port numbers and what ports are. Ports allow my computer to communicate over the network with other serrvices.
